{title: Teach Us to Number Our Days}
{subtitle: Psalm 90}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Ab] | [Bb] [Eb] [Bb/D] | [Cm] [Fm7] |
| [Bbsus4] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Lord, you have been our dwelling [Bb]place
Through [Ab]all genera[Bb]tions
Before the [Fm7]mountains were [Bb]born
From ev[Eb]erlasting to everlasting [Ab]you are God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A [Eb]thousand years [Abmaj7]in your [Bb]sight
Are like a [Ab]day that has just gone [Bb]by
Like grass that [Eb]springs up in the morn[Eb/G]ing
By [Ab]evening it [Bb]withers and dries [Eb]up
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Teach us to [Bb]number our [Eb]days
That [Ebmaj7/G]we may [Ab]gain a [Bb]heart of [Eb]wisdom
[Ab]Teach us [Bb]to number [Cm]our days
[Cm7/Bb]That we may [Ab]gain a [Bb]heart of [Eb]wisdom
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Seventy years, that is the span of our [Bb]life
Or [Ab]eighty, if [Bb]we have the strength
They pass [Eb]quickly, and [Eb/G]we fly a[Ab]way
Turn back, [Eb]LORD, have com[Ab]passion on your [Bb]servants
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Teach us to [Bb]number our [Eb]days
That [Eb/G]we may [Ab]gain a [Bb]heart of [Eb]wisdom
[Ab]Teach us [Bb]to number [Cm]our days
[Cm7/Bb]That we may [Ab]gain a [Bb]heart of [Eb]wisdom
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Satisfy [Ab]us in the morn[Bb]ing [Eb]with your stead[Bb/D]fast [Cm]love
That [Ab]we may sing for [Bb]joy and be [Eb]glad [Bb/D]all our [Cm]days
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
May the [Ab]favor of the [Bb]Lord our God [Eb]rest [Bb/D]up[Cm]on us
Es[Ab]tablish the [Bb]work of our [Eb]hands
Yes, es[Ab]tablish the [Bb]work of our [Eb]hands
{end_of_verse}
